{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/968993-lair-idea-belly-of-the-beast","id":968993,"title":"Lair idea: Belly of the Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-13T21:18:57-07:00","id":968993,"title":"Lair idea: Belly of the Beast","content":"I'm wondering, would it be possible for a Beast's lair to be somehow a representation of the inside of their body? Would I need to change anything to represent this? Would the Beast be able to manifest inside their own &quot;body&quot;, or would they interact with it by spawning proxies? <br /> <br /> I'm asking because it's a common enough trope in stories dealing with giant monsters that I think it would be an interesting basis for a lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:36:01-07:00","id":969426,"title":"","content":"One of the examples given in the section on lair traits is a Namtaru using &quot;Flooded&quot; and &quot;Corrosive&quot; to represent the digestive tract of a huge monster. It's extremely possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{